            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The sedative, analgesic, antipyretic and anti-inflammatory activities of the volatile oil isolated from the leaves of Pinus pumila are reported, the volatile oil being administered ip or po. The ip LD50 in mice was 0.577 +/- 0.056 ml/kg.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
